window.PB_SEARCH=[{"k":"Journey","t":"Launch your event app","s":"From a new app to people downloading it from the App Store and Google Play.","u":"launch/index.html","x":"Your event's own app is in the App Store and Google Play, with your name, icon, look and content, and you tried it on real phones first."},{"k":"Planner","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Plan from your event date","s":"Enter your event date, and the plan works back to the working day each step should be done by. The days are allowances you can change, and your ExpoPlatform team confirms the dates of their own steps. Working days are Monday to Friday: public holidays are not counted.","u":"launch/index.html#plan","x":"plan planner dates deadline timeline schedule Your event starts on Create the app Store set-up done Look and content ready, icon and splash picture settled First test builds sent to testers Store listing, store screenshots and demo account ready Ask ExpoPlatform to publish ExpoPlatform approves the request The stores review the builds Your ExpoPlatform team starts the rollout App in the stores Your event"},{"k":"Step 1","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Open App Studio from your ExpoPlatform admin.","s":"You see Your apps.","u":"launch/index.html#step-open","x":"App Studio opens inside your admin, on Your apps. If App Studio shows “Your session has expired - reopen App Studio from your admin”, open it again from your admin, then check and save again any change you were saving. You see Your apps. Your apps, the page App Studio opens on"},{"k":"Step 2","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Press New app, name the app, choose its events and press Create.","s":"The new app opens on its Overview.","u":"launch/index.html#step-create","x":"“It starts as a draft: nothing reaches the stores until you build and publish it.” Several events works by event tag: if no event has one, tag your events in your admin, or choose One event. Start from can copy the look and home-screen widget settings of an app you already have. The new app opens on its Overview. The New app button on Your apps"},{"k":"Step 3","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Your ExpoPlatform team sets the app up in the App Store and Google Play.","s":"Publish shows its tabs: Overview, Store listing, Releases and Rollout.","u":"launch/index.html#step-setup","x":"Creating the app sends them a set-up request; they approve it and choose the store account the app is published under. Until it is done, both build buttons are greyed out: wait, and ask your ExpoPlatform contact if you need to know where it stands. If they decline, App Studio says “ExpoPlatform did not set this app up in the stores”: ask your ExpoPlatform contact. Publish shows its tabs: Overview, Store listing, Releases and Rollout. Publish Not in the stores yet ExpoPlatform is setting this app up in the App Store and Google Play - you can build it once that is done"},{"k":"Step 4","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Set the app icon and the splash in Name, icon & splash, and press Save changes.","s":"Your icon shows in Name, icon & splash after you save.","u":"launch/index.html#step-identity","x":"The icon, the name under it, and the splash picture and its colour are built into each build of the app. The save bar says changes reach the app at the next refresh, but phones show these only once a new build is installed. In store builds, the name under the icon is the app's store name, not App name in the app. Your icon shows in Name, icon & splash after you save. Name, icon & splash"},{"k":"Step 5","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Choose how people sign in to each event, and whether new visitors can register.","s":"You pressed Save changes in Sign-in & registration.","u":"launch/index.html#step-signin","x":"You pressed Save changes in Sign-in & registration. Sign-in When people must sign in Sign-in button Scan-to-sign-in button Show the event's name on the sign-in screen"},{"k":"Step 6","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Build the menu: add the features and pages people need, section by section.","s":"The phone preview shows the menu you want, and you pressed Save changes.","u":"launch/index.html#step-menu","x":"Menu & content shows one event and one language at a time, and switching drops unsaved changes without asking: save first. The phone preview shows the menu you want, and you pressed Save changes. Section header Bottom bar Add to this section Edit Remove from the menu Add"},{"k":"Step 7","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Set each event's brand colours, light and dark, and its fonts in Colours & fonts.","s":"You pressed Save changes, and the phone preview shows your colours in light and dark.","u":"launch/index.html#step-design","x":"You pressed Save changes, and the phone preview shows your colours in light and dark. Colours & fonts"},{"k":"Step 8","j":"Launch your event app","t":"In Home screen, switch Designed home screen on, then design each event's home screen.","s":"Designed home screen is on, the phone preview shows the home screen you want, and you saved it.","u":"launch/index.html#step-home","x":"Colours, the home screen, the menu and pages reach installed apps at their next refresh: you can keep improving them after launch, with no new build. A new app starts with Designed home screen off, unless it was copied from an app where it is on. Designed home screen is on, the phone preview shows the home screen you want, and you saved it. Designed home screen, at the top of Home screen"},{"k":"Step 9","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Open Build & test and press Build for iOS, then Build for Android.","s":"Each build ends Ready and reads Store-signed; if a ready build is not Store-signed, ask your ExpoPlatform contact to add your app's store key.","u":"launch/index.html#step-build","x":"You can leave the page while a build runs, and an iOS and an Android build can run at the same time. For Android, keep App Bundle (AAB): Google Play accepts only an App Bundle. If a build runs for a long time, an amber note says it “may have stopped without telling us”: stop it and start a new one. Each build ends Ready and reads Store-signed; if a ready build is not Store-signed, ask your ExpoPlatform contact to add your app's store key. The Build & test button at the top of every page of your app"},{"k":"Step 10","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Under Send to testers, send each build to TestFlight (iPhone) or Google Play internal testing (Android).","s":"Your testers have the app: on iPhone, the send shows Live on TestFlight.","u":"launch/index.html#step-testers","x":"Apple checks a TestFlight build first, “usually within a day”, while Google Play internal testing is ready “within minutes, with no review”. Each platform takes one release at a time, store releases included: wait for one send to finish before the next. An amber Staged on Play badge means the Android release waits as a draft in Google Play Console until it is published there: ask your ExpoPlatform contact. Your testers have the app: on iPhone, the send shows Live on TestFlight. Where should the build go? TestFlight TestFlight Google Play internal testing Add testers Build Send"},{"k":"Step 11","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Install the test build from TestFlight or Google Play, or from its install link, and try every screen.","s":"You and your testers are happy with the app.","u":"launch/index.html#step-try","x":"App Studio's own advice: “Try the build on real phones before it goes to the store.” You and your testers are happy with the app. Build & test Live on TestFlight"},{"k":"Step 12","j":"Launch your event app","t":"In Publish, on Store listing, write the texts for each language and save each one.","s":"Every language you need is saved.","u":"launch/index.html#step-texts","x":"A screenshot capture takes one pass per language of your store listing, or English when it has none: add your languages first. Google Play does not get these texts from App Studio, and neither store gets What's new: ask your ExpoPlatform contact how your texts reach Google Play. Every language you need is saved. Add a language App name Short description Description What's new Save English"},{"k":"Step 13","j":"Launch your event app","t":"In Store screenshots, take the screenshots, make store artwork in Store studio, and attach it to your listing.","s":"See them in Publish shows the pictures on your listing.","u":"launch/index.html#step-shots","x":"When the app has no screenshot build for that store yet, Take screenshots builds the app first, so it too waits for the store set-up. Your Store studio set is held only in the page: attach it before you leave or reload the page. See them in Publish shows the pictures on your listing. Listing language Attach to the store listing"},{"k":"Step 14","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Under Store review, give the store reviewers a demo account, and press Save demo account.","s":"App Studio says “Demo account saved”.","u":"launch/index.html#step-demo","x":"The store reviewers sign in to your app with it, and it is the only set-up step that is yours. Without it, the iPhone submission fails and the release stays Ready. Pick a demo event with real sessions and exhibitors: the review check looks for at least 3 sessions on its agenda. Notes for the reviewers are kept in App Studio, but not sent with your submissions. App Studio says “Demo account saved”. Demo login Demo password Demo event number Notes for the reviewers Save demo account"},{"k":"Step 15","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Open Publish and read each store's card and What now.","s":"Set up, Build and Test read Done on both store cards, and Store listing reads Done or, before the app's first release, What now says “Your listing goes to [store] with your publication”.","u":"launch/index.html#step-check","x":"Each store card shows six steps (Set up, Build, Test, Store listing, Publish and Live) and who acts next: Your move, Our team is on it or The store is on it. Set up, Build and Test read Done on both store cards, and Store listing reads Done or, before the app's first release, What now says “Your listing goes to [store] with your publication”. App Store Your listing goes to App Store with your publication ExpoPlatform sends it when they approve your request to publish. Open releases"},{"k":"Step 16","j":"Launch your event app","t":"On Releases, press Submit to the stores, keep each store's newest build, and press Submit.","s":"App Studio says “Sent to ExpoPlatform for approval”, or “Sent to the stores” for an app that needs no approval.","u":"launch/index.html#step-submit","x":"One request can wait at a time: Submit to the stores is greyed out until ExpoPlatform decides. App Studio says “Sent to ExpoPlatform for approval”, or “Sent to the stores” for an app that needs no approval. App Store Build Google Play Build Close Submit"},{"k":"Step 17","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Your ExpoPlatform team approves the request.","s":"Releases says “Approved [when]: [the builds] went to the stores' review. Follow it below.”","u":"launch/index.html#step-approve","x":"When they approve, your store listing is sent, and each build goes on to its store's review. A declined request reads “Declined: [reason]”, or “Declined: no reason given”: sort out what the reason names and submit again, or ask your ExpoPlatform contact when no reason is given. Releases says “Approved [when]: [the builds] went to the stores' review. Follow it below.” Releases Waiting for ExpoPlatform approval: App Store [version], Google Play [version], sent [when]."},{"k":"Step 18","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Apple and Google review the release. Follow it on Releases.","s":"The release reads Approved.","u":"launch/index.html#step-review","x":"Apple typically reviews 90% of submissions in less than 48 hours; for certain developer accounts, Google Play's review can take up to seven days, or longer in exceptional cases. If a store turns the release down, its card shows the store's message when it gave one, and a new release goes through Submit to the stores and ExpoPlatform's approval again. If your event is close and the iPhone version is still in review, your ExpoPlatform team can ask Apple to expedite the review, and Apple decides. The release reads Approved. Draft Uploading Processing Ready Submitted In review Approved Rolling out Live"},{"k":"Step 19","j":"Launch your event app","t":"The app rolls out to people.","s":"The release reads Live.","u":"launch/index.html#step-rollout","x":"Apple releases an app's first iPhone version on approval, and Android's first 5% stage goes out by itself; the rest waits for your ExpoPlatform team, who start the rollout. The Overview can still read Not in the stores yet when people can already download the app: Your apps shows the live version. The release reads Live. Rollout Rolling out The rollout moves on only while the app stays healthy."},{"k":"Step 20","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Keep improving the app: save, and installed apps pick it up.","s":"You know which changes need a new version.","u":"launch/index.html#step-changes","x":"You know which changes need a new version. No new build Colours, home screen, menu and pages: at the next refresh Sign-in settings: at the next refresh Texts in Translations: within about 30 minutes Needs a new build and store release The app icon The name under the icon (in store builds, the store name) The splash picture and its colour Switching a home-screen widget on or off"},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Launch your event app","t":"The build buttons are greyed out","s":"Read the note above the list: while the set-up runs, wait, and ask your ExpoPlatform contact if you need to know where it stands; if it says “ExpoPlatform did not set this app up in the stores”, ask your ExpoPlatform contact.","u":"launch/index.html#sym-1","x":"ExpoPlatform has not finished setting the app up in the stores, or did not set it up."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Publish says “Not in the stores yet”","s":"Read the line under it: while your request waits, wait until the set-up is done; once ExpoPlatform is putting your app in the stores, ask your ExpoPlatform contact if this takes longer than a working day; if they did not set it up, ask your ExpoPlatform contact.","u":"launch/index.html#sym-2","x":"The store set-up is not finished."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Launch your event app","t":"My new icon, name, splash picture or widget does not show on phones","s":"For the icon, the splash picture and its colour or a widget switch, make a new build, install it and publish it; for the name in store builds, ask your ExpoPlatform contact.","u":"launch/index.html#sym-3","x":"They reach phones only with a new build, and so does switching a widget on or off; in store builds, the name under the icon is the store name, not App name in the app."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Launch your event app","t":"The phone preview does not open on my designed home","s":"Switch Designed home screen on and press Save home screen, or choose Home in the Preview strip.","u":"launch/index.html#sym-4","x":"Designed home screen is off (“When off, the app opens on its first menu screen and this design is not used.”), or the Preview strip below the form starts the preview on My Badge or Boot flow."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Launch your event app","t":"A build has been running for a long time","s":"Stop it and start a new one. If your builds keep failing, ask your ExpoPlatform contact.","u":"launch/index.html#sym-5","x":"It may have stopped: an amber note on its card says so."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Launch your event app","t":"A choice in Send to testers is greyed out","s":"Read the reason the dialog gives and do what it says; if new builds are not Store-signed, or a release waits as a draft in Google Play Console, ask your ExpoPlatform contact; while another release is still moving, wait until it has finished.","u":"launch/index.html#sym-6","x":"The app is not in that store yet, there is no Store-signed build of that platform, another release of that platform is still moving (a store release included), or, on Android, an earlier release waits as a draft or the newest build is already on another Google Play track."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Launch your event app","t":"Submit to the stores is greyed out","s":"Wait for their decision; it shows on Releases.","u":"launch/index.html#sym-7","x":"A request is already waiting for ExpoPlatform."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Launch your event app","t":"A release is stuck at Ready","s":"Open Store review in Publish and fix each item marked Your move; items marked Our team are your ExpoPlatform team's.","u":"launch/index.html#sym-8","x":"Store review still has something to sort out, such as a missing demo account, a demo account the check cannot sign in with, or a demo event that looks empty."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Launch your event app","t":"A store turned the release down","s":"Fix it, build again if needed, and ask again with Submit to the stores: the new release goes through ExpoPlatform's approval and the store's review again.","u":"launch/index.html#sym-9","x":"The store found a problem; its card shows the store's message when it gave one."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Launch your event app","t":"The Overview says “Not in the stores yet”, but people can download the app","s":"Check the live version on Your apps.","u":"launch/index.html#sym-10","x":"The Overview counts a store as live only from App Studio's own store record."},{"k":"Journey","t":"Make the app look like your event","s":"From your event's brand to an app that shows it, event by event and language by language.","u":"look/index.html","x":"Each event shows your colours, fonts, home screen and pages, the app's texts carry your wording, and installed apps pick it all up with no new build."},{"k":"Step 1","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Decide what each event needs: colours, fonts, the home screen and pages are set event by event.","s":"You know what to set for each event, and what is the same for every event.","u":"look/index.html#step-levels","x":"Texts are kept per language too: the home's header and block texts, and each page's title, tab names, texts and HTML. You will not find the design style, the tab bar style or whether people may pick their own style in App Studio: your ExpoPlatform team sets them, so ask your ExpoPlatform contact. You know what to set for each event, and what is the same for every event. Set for each event Colours, light and dark, fonts, pictures and the missing-picture choice The home screen's layout, top bar, header, blocks and badge pictures Custom pages, each with its tabs and blocks The same for every event Designed home screen, on or off The event picker's colours and fonts, in apps with several events Your wording in Translations, kept per language"},{"k":"Step 2","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"In Colours & fonts, keep Light on and set the event's brand colours, or start from a palette.","s":"Each colour you set shows Use default under it.","u":"look/index.html#step-brand","x":"A palette fills all 21 colours of the scheme you are on, as a one-time fill you then adjust. With several events, pick the event in the Colours header first: each event has its own colours. Each colour must be a #RRGGBB code, or nothing is saved when you press Save changes. Each colour you set shows Use default under it. Colours & fonts: Start from a palette, then the Brand colours"},{"k":"Step 3","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Press Dark at the top of Colours, and set only the colours that should differ in dark mode.","s":"With Dark on, the phone preview is dark too, and the fields hold your dark colours.","u":"look/index.html#step-dark","x":"The phone preview turns dark with it, and each empty field shows the light colour it falls back to. A palette fills the scheme you are on: press Dark first to fill the dark set with one. With Dark on, the phone preview is dark too, and the fields hold your dark colours. Colours In dark mode, a colour you leave empty uses its light one."},{"k":"Step 4","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Choose the fonts under Fonts and the pictures under Pictures, then press Save changes.","s":"You pressed Save changes, and a green message confirmed it.","u":"look/index.html#step-fonts","x":"One Save changes saves the whole draft: every event's colours, fonts and pictures, and Name, icon & splash too. In an app with several events, colour the screen where people choose an event in the Event picker block, above Colours: it is one set for the whole app. A picture is stored as soon as you upload it, but the app uses it only after Save changes. You pressed Save changes, and a green message confirmed it. Fonts: Headings and Body text"},{"k":"Step 5","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"In Home screen, switch Designed home screen on, and pick the event if your app has several.","s":"Designed home screen is on, and the phone preview, started on Home, opens on the designed home.","u":"look/index.html#step-home-on","x":"It is one switch for the whole app: “When off, the app opens on its first menu screen and this design is not used.” A new app starts with this switch off, unless it was copied from an app where it is on: check it before you design. Designed home screen is on, and the phone preview, started on Home, opens on the designed home. Designed home screen, at the top of Home screen"},{"k":"Step 6","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Choose the event's Layout, then what the Top bar shows: its top-right button, the search and the event name.","s":"The phone preview shows the layout and the top bar you chose.","u":"look/index.html#step-layout","x":"Layouts carry no colours of their own: “Colours come from Colours & fonts.” An AI assistant button in the top right appears only once the assistant is ready for this event: follow Preparation on the AI Synapsium block. Whether the AI assistant is switched on for your app at all is your ExpoPlatform team's choice: ask your ExpoPlatform contact. The phone preview shows the layout and the top bar you chose. Layout, below the Home screen block"},{"k":"Step 7","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Under Header, write the line above the title and the title, pressing each language button you need.","s":"A dot marks each language that has a text.","u":"look/index.html#step-header","x":"A text you leave empty uses the default: “Welcome, [name]” above the title, and “Your Digital Future Starts Here.” as the title. A line written in DE, FR, ES, IT or RU needs an English text too, or the save is refused. A dot marks each language that has a text. Header: Line above the title and Title, with a button for each language"},{"k":"Step 8","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Under Header picture, add a picture or a video and your logo, and set the tint over the picture or video.","s":"Picture (4:3) or Video shows yours, with Replace and Use default under it.","u":"look/index.html#step-picture","x":"The tint lies over the picture or video and keeps the words readable. Tint over the picture stays greyed until there is a picture or a video: add one first. Pictures and the video are stored as soon as you upload them, and the home uses them after Save home screen. Picture (4:3) or Video shows yours, with Replace and Use default under it. Header picture: Picture (4:3) and Video"},{"k":"Step 9","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Add, order and switch the home's blocks, choose who sees each, then press Save home screen.","s":"App Studio says “Content saved — live on the next app fetch”.","u":"look/index.html#step-blocks","x":"Save home screen saves in one go the home of every event you edited since the last save. The bin takes a block off the list at once, without asking: to hide a block and keep its settings, switch it off instead. Restore the default home is saved straight away, without Save home screen: “Every change to this home will be lost.” To give people a panel on their phone's own home screen, use Home-screen widgets, not blocks: switching a widget on or off needs a new build. App Studio says “Content saved — live on the next app fetch”. Blocks: each row has a handle, a switch, a chevron and a bin"},{"k":"Step 10","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"In Custom pages, press New page, then Write a page, and give the page a title and blocks.","s":"The save bar lists nothing to fix.","u":"look/index.html#step-page","x":"Besides Text, a page takes most of the Home screen's blocks, with the same settings. Each page belongs to one event: with several events, pick the event beside Your pages first. What you write stays in this browser tab until Save page, and closing the tab loses it. Who sees it decides what the app shows but does not protect the page: “everything on a page can be read by anyone who has your app.” The save bar lists nothing to fix. New page Write a page Add a built-in screen"},{"k":"Step 11","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Under Language you are writing in, press another language, and write the title, tab names and text in it.","s":"In each language you need, no Text block's row says it has no text in that language.","u":"look/index.html#step-page-lang","x":"As App Studio's hint says, “English shows wherever a language is left empty.” The title, and any tab you name, need English, and every Text block English text or a picture: write the page in English first. Your own HTML is written per language, so write it, links included, in each language. In each language you need, no Text block's row says it has no text in that language. Title (English) Language you are writing in EN DE FR ES IT RU Add to the menu when saved"},{"k":"Step 12","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Press Save page, then arrange the page's place in the menu in Menu & content.","s":"App Studio confirms with the page's English title, then “added to Event — live on the next app refresh”, or “saved — it is not in the menu yet” with Add to the menu when saved off.","u":"look/index.html#step-page-save","x":"With Add to the menu when saved on, a new page goes to the end of the Event section of the event's menu. If Menu & content is already open in another tab, reload it before you save there, or its save takes the page out of the menu again. A page saved with Add to the menu when saved off is listed under Not in the menu: press Add to menu there. App Studio confirms with the page's English title, then “added to Event — live on the next app refresh”, or “saved — it is not in the menu yet” with Add to the menu when saved off. Custom pages Live on the next app refresh. No new build needed."},{"k":"Step 13","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"In Translations, choose the Language, find the text, type your wording beside it, and save.","s":"App Studio says “Saved. Installed apps pick the texts up within about 30 minutes.”","u":"look/index.html#step-wording","x":"No build is started: “Installed apps pick up saved texts within about 30 minutes.” Sign-in and registration button texts and menu names are not here: word them per event in Sign-in & registration and Menu & content. Language is locked while you have unsaved changes: save them, or undo them, before you switch. App Studio says “Saved. Installed apps pick the texts up within about 30 minutes.” Translations Change any text the app shows, in each language. Leave a field empty to keep the standard text. No new build is needed."},{"k":"Step 14","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Tick Changed only to list the texts that carry your wording, and check each language you offer.","s":"The count line under the search box says how many texts carry your wording.","u":"look/index.html#step-wording-check","x":"Your wording is kept per language, so each language is checked and changed on its own. If Language does not list a language you need, ask your ExpoPlatform contact: your ExpoPlatform team switches languages on. A text a language lacks reads “No standard text”, and the app shows the English text there unless you type your own wording. The count line under the search box says how many texts carry your wording. Language English (en) Search: sign in, agenda, my badge… Changed only"},{"k":"Step 15","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"In the phone preview, check each event in light and dark, and, on Home, as a signed-in person and a guest.","s":"Each event reads well in light and dark, for guests and for signed-in people.","u":"look/index.html#step-preview","x":"With several events, the preview follows the event you pick in Home screen or Custom pages. App Studio checks only Tertiary on Primary, so check that every other button and text stays readable, in both themes. After Use default, the preview keeps showing the saved colour, font or picture until you save. Translations has no preview: installed apps show your saved wording within about 30 minutes. Each event reads well in light and dark, for guests and for signed-in people. The Preview strip below the form: Signed-in preview or Guest preview"},{"k":"Step 16","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Keep the look up to date: what you save reaches installed apps with no new build.","s":"You know when each change reaches installed apps: once a build of this app is installed, it shows your look after its next refresh, and your wording within about 30 minutes.","u":"look/index.html#step-reach","x":"Most sections say it in their save bar: “Changes reach the app the next time it refreshes.” Save changes also saves Name, icon & splash: its icon, the name under the icon (in store builds, the store name) and the splash picture and colour reach phones only after the next build is installed. You know when each change reaches installed apps: once a build of this app is installed, it shows your look after its next refresh, and your wording within about 30 minutes. At the next refresh Colours, fonts and pictures, after Save changes The home screen, after Save home screen Custom pages, after Save page Within about 30 minutes Your wording, after the save button in Translations The app checks for new texts at most once every 30 minutes"},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"“Text on this colour is hard to read ([ratio]:1).” shows under Primary","s":"Press the button beside it, which reads Use and a darker colour's code, or change Primary or Tertiary; the note is advice, and saving is not blocked.","u":"look/index.html#sym-1","x":"The Tertiary colour on your Primary colour has a contrast below 4.5:1."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"After Save changes, a red message says a colour must be a #RRGGBB code","s":"Correct it to # followed by six characters from 0 to 9 and a to f, then press Save changes again.","u":"look/index.html#sym-2","x":"A colour is not a #RRGGBB code, so nothing was saved."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"The phone preview does not open on my designed home","s":"Switch Designed home screen on and press Save home screen, or choose Home in the Preview strip.","u":"look/index.html#sym-3","x":"Designed home screen is off (“When off, the app opens on its first menu screen and this design is not used.”), or the Preview strip below the form starts the preview on My Badge or Boot flow."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"After Save home screen, a red message shows, and nothing is saved","s":"Correct what the message names, then press Save home screen again.","u":"look/index.html#sym-4","x":"A block's settings break its rules, a header Text colour is not a #RRGGBB code, or a header line in another language has no English text."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Save page is off, with lines listed above it","s":"Fix each line listed, for example an English title of 1 to 40 characters, and English text or a picture in each Text block.","u":"look/index.html#sym-5","x":"The page breaks a rule, such as a title or a Text block without English: “Fix what is listed above to save.”"},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Saving a page says “This page was changed by someone else — reload it before saving”","s":"Copy any text you want to keep, reload the page, open your page again and make your changes again.","u":"look/index.html#sym-6","x":"Someone else, such as your ExpoPlatform team, saved the page after you opened it."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"My new page is not in the menu","s":"Press Add to menu under Not in the menu; if the Event section is full, make room there, in Menu & content.","u":"look/index.html#sym-7","x":"It was saved with Add to the menu when saved off, or a save in Menu & content, open in another tab, took it out."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"Language is locked in Translations","s":"Save your changes, or undo each one, then choose the language.","u":"look/index.html#sym-8","x":"You have unsaved changes: “Save your changes before switching the language”."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Make the app look like your event","t":"My new wording does not show on phones yet","s":"Allow about 30 minutes, check on a phone with a build of this app installed, and set your wording in each language people use; if App Studio said texts could not be saved, press the save button again.","u":"look/index.html#sym-9","x":"A phone with a build of this app installed picks up saved texts within about 30 minutes, and your wording is kept per language."},{"k":"Journey","t":"Let people sign in and register","s":"From your app's events to a sign-in screen that lets people in the way your event works.","u":"sign-in/index.html","x":"Your app signs people in to each event the way your event works, with your button texts and sign-in pictures, and lets new visitors register if you want it to."},{"k":"Step 1","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"In Events & updates, check which events the app offers, and press Save changes if you change them.","s":"The events your app should offer are chosen, and App Studio says “Saved” after a change.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-events","x":"Until the app's events are chosen here, Sign-in & registration shows only a message asking you to choose them. For Several events, by event tag, your events need tags in your ExpoPlatform admin, and App Studio saves only with at least one tag ticked. Saving here also writes the choice of events to your ExpoPlatform admin, which gives the app its list of events. The events your app should offer are chosen, and App Studio says “Saved” after a change. The app is for Several events, by event tag Event tags"},{"k":"Step 2","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"Open Sign-in & registration and choose the event in Event.","s":"The event's settings show, starting with Signing in.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-open","x":"Each event has its own settings, which start from its values in the old App Builder. Later changes in the old App Builder no longer reach your App Studio app: make them here. The event's settings show, starting with Signing in. Sign-in & registration, in the App group of the menu on the left"},{"k":"Step 3","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"In Signing in, choose Sign-in: In the app, On a web page or Both.","s":"The phone preview shows the sign-in screen with your choice.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-mode","x":"In the app signs people in with the app's own form, On a web page sends them to a web page, and Both offers both, with a second button. With Web sign-in address left empty, people sign in on the event's own sign-in page; an address over 2000 characters is refused when you save. The phone preview shows the sign-in screen with your choice. Sign-in Both Web sign-in address When people must sign in Sign-in button Web sign-in button Scan-to-sign-in button Show the event's name on the sign-in screen"},{"k":"Step 4","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"Choose When people must sign in: Right after choosing the event or When they open their account.","s":"When people must sign in shows the choice your event needs.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-when","x":"With Right after choosing the event, people sign in before they enter the event; otherwise they enter as guests and can sign in later from the side menu. The preview always opens on the sign-in screen, whichever you choose. When people must sign in shows the choice your event needs. Sign-in In the app When people must sign in Sign-in button Scan-to-sign-in button Show the event's name on the sign-in screen"},{"k":"Step 5","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"Write the Sign-in button and Scan-to-sign-in button texts, and for Both, the Web sign-in button.","s":"The phone preview shows your texts on the buttons it shows.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-texts","x":"The app's sign-in screen shows them on its buttons, in each language you save them in. Each takes up to 30 characters; left empty, the buttons read “Log in”, “Scan login” and “Log in with SSO”. A language you never saved them in shows the English text, else the first language written: save them in each language your visitors use. The scan button shows only when sign-in by scanning a badge is on for the event. The phone preview shows your texts on the buttons it shows. Sign-in Both Web sign-in address When people must sign in Sign-in button Web sign-in button Scan-to-sign-in button Show the event's name on the sign-in screen"},{"k":"Step 6","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"Switch Show the event's name on the sign-in screen on or off.","s":"The phone preview shows the top of the sign-in screen the way you want it.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-name","x":"With the switch off, the sign-in screen shows no event name, dates or logo at the top. The phone preview shows the top of the sign-in screen the way you want it. Sign-in In the app When people must sign in Sign-in button Scan-to-sign-in button Show the event's name on the sign-in screen"},{"k":"Step 7","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"In Registration, switch on Show the register button, give it a text and choose Registration happens.","s":"The phone preview shows the register button with your text.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-register","x":"The button opens the event's own registration page, or the Registration website you enter for Another website. The button shows only while the switch is on and there is a registration address to open. Its text is kept per language, up to 30 characters; left empty, it reads “Registration”. The phone preview shows the register button with your text. Show the register button Register button Registration happens Another website Registration website"},{"k":"Step 8","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"For the app's own registration form instead of the web page, switch on Native registration form.","s":"Native registration form is switched on.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-native","x":"On events with the new registration switched on, the sign-in screen's “Registration” button and “Sign up” link then open the app's own form. It is for the whole app, and it shows only while Show the register button is on and Registration happens is The event's registration page. The new registration is a setting of each event, not one in App Studio: events without it keep the registration web page. It is saved first: if that fails, a red message shows and the event's settings are not saved either. Native registration form is switched on. Show the register button Register button Registration happens The event's registration page Native registration form"},{"k":"Step 9","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"Under Features, choose whether people see their badge while the event's data downloads after sign-in.","s":"The badge switch is set the way you want it for this event.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-badge","x":"With Show the participant's badge as the loading screen on, the person's digital badge fades in over the loading screen while the event's data downloads. It is not for exhibitor company owners, and it shows only when the person has a QR code. AI meeting notes, in the same block, is for the whole app: switch it only if you mean every event. The badge switch is set the way you want it for this event. Show the participant's badge as the loading screen Ring around QR codes Scan badges by reading the printed text (OCR) AI meeting notes"},{"k":"Step 10","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"Check the sign-in screen in the phone beside the form, then press Save changes.","s":"App Studio says “Saved”.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-preview","x":"The phone shows the event's sign-in screen as a signed-out visitor sees it, with your unsaved changes. If you see no phone, widen the window: the preview shows only on wide screens. The preview draws the event's stored logo, list background and sign-in button colours, which this section has no field to change. App Studio says “Saved”. Sign-in & registration Saved The sign-in screen as a signed-out visitor sees it. Saved changes reach the app itself. Changes reach the app the next time it refreshes."},{"k":"Step 11","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"Repeat the button texts for each language, and the whole section for each event.","s":"Every event, and every language your visitors use, is saved.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-repeat","x":"Each event keeps its own settings, chosen in Event, and only the button texts are kept per language, chosen in Language of the texts. Switching the event or the language drops unsaved edits without asking: save first. The sign-in mode, the addresses and the switches hold one value for every language: changing one under any language changes it for all. Native registration form and AI meeting notes are for the whole app, not only the event you are editing. Every event, and every language your visitors use, is saved. Event Language of the texts"},{"k":"Step 12","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"In Colours & fonts, under Pictures, set the Login background, Login logo and Home / loading backdrop.","s":"Each picture you set says “Your picture.”, and you pressed Save changes.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-pictures","x":"Pictures is for “The sign-in screen and the backdrop shown while the home screen loads.” With several events, pick the event in the Colours header first. A picture is stored as soon as you upload it, but the app uses it only after Save changes, which also saves Name, icon & splash. To see the sign-in screen in the phone, choose Boot flow below the form: it walks through the splash, login and choose event. Each picture you set says “Your picture.”, and you pressed Save changes. Pictures, in Colours & fonts"},{"k":"Step 13","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"If guests can enter, set View as to Guest (not signed in) in Menu & content and tap through each event's menu.","s":"Seen as a guest, each event's menu holds what you want people to see before they sign in.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-guests","x":"A menu item with anything ticked under Visible for is not shown to people who are not signed in. On the Home screen, each block's Who sees it is Everyone, Guests only or Signed-in only: check it with Guest preview. On a page from Custom pages, Who sees it decides what the app shows but does not protect the page: “everything on a page can be read by anyone who has your app.” After you pick another event in Event, set View as to Guest (not signed in) again: it starts on Visitor. Seen as a guest, each event's menu holds what you want people to see before they sign in. View as Guest (not signed in)"},{"k":"Step 14","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"Check the sign-in screen on a phone with a build of this app installed, once the app has refreshed.","s":"The phone's sign-in screen shows your texts, buttons and pictures.","u":"sign-in/index.html#step-phones","x":"Sign-in settings and pictures reach installed builds of this app with no new build or store release. Only saved changes reach phones, while the previews also show unsaved ones. Your old apps never show what you save here: a phone shows it only once a build of this app is installed, a test build from Build & test first. The phone's sign-in screen shows your texts, buttons and pictures. No new build Sign-in & registration: at the next refresh Colours & fonts, with the sign-in pictures: at the next refresh Menu & content and Home screen: at the next refresh Needs a new build and store release The app icon The name under the icon (in store builds, the store name) The splash picture and its colour Switching a home-screen widget on or off"},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"Sign-in & registration asks you to choose the events in Events & updates first","s":"In Events & updates, choose the event or the event tags and save, then choose an event in Event.","u":"sign-in/index.html#sym-1","x":"No event is chosen for the app yet, and these settings are kept per event."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"Events & updates says “No event has a tag yet. Tag your events in your admin first.”","s":"Tag your events in your ExpoPlatform admin, then come back.","u":"sign-in/index.html#sym-2","x":"Several events, by event tag is chosen, and no event in your ExpoPlatform admin has a tag yet."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"My changes disappeared when I picked another event or language","s":"Make the changes again, and save before you switch.","u":"sign-in/index.html#sym-3","x":"In Menu & content, Sign-in & registration and Events & updates, switching the event or the language drops unsaved changes without asking."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"A change I made under one language shows in every language","s":"Set those once for each event, and write only the button texts in each language.","u":"sign-in/index.html#sym-4","x":"Only the button texts are kept per language; the sign-in mode, the addresses and the switches hold one value for every language."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"The register button does not show on the sign-in screen","s":"Switch it on and save; with Another website, fill in Registration website, and with The event's registration page, the event needs a registration page of its own to open.","u":"sign-in/index.html#sym-5","x":"It shows only while Show the register button is on and there is a registration address to open."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"Saving says “This could not be saved - try again” or “Reopen App Studio from your admin”","s":"For the first, press Save changes again; for the second, open App Studio again from your ExpoPlatform admin and make the change again.","u":"sign-in/index.html#sym-6","x":"The first means the save did not go through, and your edits stay in the form; the second means your App Studio session has ended."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"There is no phone beside the form, or it shows “Loading the preview…” or “The app's config could not be loaded…”","s":"Use a wider window; if it stays loading, wait a moment, then open the section again; for the second message, try again in a minute.","u":"sign-in/index.html#sym-7","x":"The preview shows only on wide screens and can stay loading when its data is refused; the second message means the preview could not get what it needs to start."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"The sign-in screen still shows the old pictures","s":"In Colours & fonts, with the right event picked, set them under Pictures, press Save changes, and check them there with Boot flow.","u":"sign-in/index.html#sym-8","x":"Sign-in & registration cannot change them, and its preview draws the event's stored ones; Colours & fonts sets them, and the app uses them only after Save changes there."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Let people sign in and register","t":"Phones still show the old sign-in screen","s":"Check that you saved each event and language you changed, and that the phone has a build of this app, such as a test build from Build & test; it then shows them at its next refresh.","u":"sign-in/index.html#sym-9","x":"Installed apps show saved changes the next time they refresh, and only saved changes reach them; your old apps never show them."},{"k":"Journey","t":"Build the menu and content","s":"From each event's menu in App Studio to the features and pages people find in the app.","u":"menu/index.html","x":"Each event's menu holds the features and pages each kind of person needs, named, ordered and shown to the right people, and installed builds of this app show it at their next refresh."},{"k":"Step 1","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"If you wrote pages in Custom pages, press Add to menu on each one listed under Not in the menu.","s":"The page's row reads In the menu.","u":"menu/index.html#step-your-page","x":"It goes to the end of the Event section at once, and installed builds of this app show it on their next refresh, with no new build. If Menu & content is already open in another tab, reload it before you save there, or its save takes the page out of the menu again. In Menu & content, a page listed as “Page title” has no name yet: press Edit and name it, or the menu cannot be saved. The page's row reads In the menu. Add to menu Edit"},{"k":"Step 2","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"Open Menu & content, pick the event in Event, and the language if your app has more than one.","s":"Menu & content shows that event's menu, with its names in that language.","u":"menu/index.html#step-open","x":"Switching the event or the language drops unsaved changes without asking: press Save changes first. Language of the texts starts on English each time the section opens: pick your language before you edit its texts. Change this app's menu here from now on: later changes in the old App Builder no longer reach it, and nothing you save here changes your old apps. Menu & content shows that event's menu, with its names in that language. Menu & content, in the menu of sections on the left"},{"k":"Step 3","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"In a section, choose a feature, A custom page or A documents page in Add to this section, and press Add.","s":"The new item is the last row of its section, unsaved until you press Save in its window or Save changes.","u":"menu/index.html#step-add-item","x":"The item goes at the end of the section with its own name and icon, seen by everyone who sees the section, and not in the bottom bar. Add to this section offers only the features switched on for the event and not already in the section. Save in an item's window saves the whole menu at once, with every other unsaved change on the page. If people already use this app, fill a new page and set Visible for in its window before you save. The new item is the last row of its section, unsaved until you press Save in its window or Save changes. Section header Add to this section Add"},{"k":"Step 4","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"Press Edit on a custom page, fill its tabs, or switch Open a web page instead on, and press Save.","s":"App Studio says “Saved”, and the item's window closes.","u":"menu/index.html#step-custom-page","x":"A custom page holds your own tabs, with their names, titles, texts and backgrounds, or a web page that opens in their place. Web page address has no format check in App Studio, so check the address before you save. Remove the tab removes a tab at once, without asking. A page built with the old App Builder's blocks opens as “Text (HTML)” and stays HTML, to keep every block. App Studio says “Saved”, and the item's window closes. Open a web page instead Tab name Title Text Background colour Background picture Add a tab"},{"k":"Step 5","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"Press Edit on a documents page, add each file with Add a document (PDF, Word, Excel), and press Save.","s":"App Studio says “Saved”, and the item's window closes.","u":"menu/index.html#step-documents","x":"The page lists each document under the name in its box, which starts as the file's name without its extension. A file uploads as soon as you choose it, but joins the page only when you press Save. Remove takes a document off the page at once, without asking. App Studio says “Saved”, and the item's window closes. Document 1 Add a document (PDF, Word, Excel) Open Remove"},{"k":"Step 6","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"If the menu has a contacts page, press Edit on it, add each person with Add a contact, and press Save.","s":"App Studio says “Saved”, and the item's window closes.","u":"menu/index.html#step-contacts","x":"Phone and Email are not checked for format, so check each one before you save. Remove takes a contact off at once, without asking. App Studio says “Saved”, and the item's window closes. Group Job title First name Last name Phone Email Photo Add a contact"},{"k":"Step 7","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"On a social media item, press Edit, tick the networks under Show these social networks, and press Save.","s":"App Studio says “Saved”, and the item's window closes.","u":"menu/index.html#step-social","x":"The item carries only the networks you tick: Facebook, LinkedIn, X (Twitter), YouTube or Pinterest. On a newly added item none is ticked, so it carries no network until you tick one. App Studio says “Saved”, and the item's window closes. Show these social networks"},{"k":"Step 8","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"Name each section in Section header, order its items with Move up and Move down, and press Save changes.","s":"On a wide screen, the preview's menu shows your headers and order, and App Studio said “Saved”.","u":"menu/index.html#step-order","x":"In the app's menu, the header is the section's title, and the section lists its items in your order. Items move only within their own section. A section header you empty and save stays empty. On a wide screen, the preview's menu shows your headers and order, and App Studio said “Saved”. Section header Bottom bar Move up Move down Edit Remove from the menu"},{"k":"Step 9","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"Press Edit on an item, change its Name in the menu and its Icon, and press Save.","s":"App Studio says “Saved”, and the item's window closes.","u":"menu/index.html#step-names","x":"The name is the item's title in the app's menu, and on its tab when it is in the bottom bar. Names are kept per language: rename the item in each language, and save before you switch. An icon you upload must be a PNG: App Studio refuses a JPEG. App Studio says “Saved”, and the item's window closes. Name in the menu Icon Cancel Save"},{"k":"Step 10","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"Switch Bottom bar on for up to four items, in the order you want the tabs, and press Save changes.","s":"The line above the sections counts the places used, out of four, and App Studio said “Saved”.","u":"menu/index.html#step-tabs","x":"In the app, the items become tabs of the bottom bar, beside the menu button, for the people who can see each item. The tabs follow the order in which you switched them on, not the items' places: to reorder them, switch them off and on again. A hidden item with Bottom bar on still takes one of the four places. The line above the sections counts the places used, out of four, and App Studio said “Saved”. Bottom bar Move up Move down Edit Remove from the menu"},{"k":"Step 11","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"Press Edit on an item, tick who should see it under Visible for, and press Save.","s":"The item's row reads “Limited to some people”.","u":"menu/index.html#step-audience","x":"The item then shows only to the signed-in people your ticks match. Once anything is ticked, people who are not signed in no longer see the item, even with All visitors ticked. If you tick exhibitor choices, check the menu with View as set to Exhibitor (company owner) after you save. The item's row reads “Limited to some people”. Name in the menu Visible for Hide this item Cancel Save"},{"k":"Step 12","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"In a custom page's window, switch Only for people who are not signed in on, and press Save.","s":"In the preview, on a wide screen, the page shows with View as set to Guest (not signed in), and not as a Visitor.","u":"menu/index.html#step-guests","x":"Signed-in people no longer see the page in the app's menu; people who are not signed in do. The switch is offered only for custom pages in the “Event (everyone)” section; for a page from Custom pages, listed as “Your page”, Who sees it on its blocks there can show each block to guests only. In the preview, on a wide screen, the page shows with View as set to Guest (not signed in), and not as a Visitor. Name in the menu Visible for Hide this item Only for people who are not signed in Cancel Save"},{"k":"Step 13","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"To keep an item in App Studio but out of the app, switch Hide this item on in its window and press Save.","s":"The item's row reads “Hidden”.","u":"menu/index.html#step-hide","x":"The app then leaves the item out completely: no menu row, no tab, no tile. Remove from the menu does not ask first: once you save, the item is gone from this event's menu in every language, with its content. The item's row reads “Hidden”. Name in the menu Visible for Hide this item Cancel Save"},{"k":"Step 14","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"In the phone preview, pick each kind of person in View as, then open the menu and tap through it.","s":"The phone preview shows the menu you want for each kind of person.","u":"menu/index.html#step-preview","x":"View as offers Guest (not signed in), Visitor, Exhibitor (company owner), Team member, Speaker and Moderator, and saves nothing. The preview shows only on wide screens. A change made in an item's window shows in the preview only after you press Save there, which saves it at once. The phone preview shows the menu you want for each kind of person. Menu & content Open the menu in the phone to see your changes. Saved changes reach the app itself."},{"k":"Step 15","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"Press Save changes, then add the texts in each other language, and build each other event's menu in Event.","s":"App Studio says “Saved” for each event's menu, in each language.","u":"menu/index.html#step-save","x":"Installed builds of this app show the saved menu the next time they refresh, with no new build. Your ExpoPlatform team can also change an event's menu: what they save shows in Menu & content, and what you save is what the app shows. A document, a picture or an icon of your own is stored as soon as it is uploaded, even if the menu is never saved. Your old apps never show what you save here: a phone shows it only once a build of this app is installed, a test build from Build & test first. App Studio says “Saved” for each event's menu, in each language. Menu & content Saved Changes reach the app the next time it refreshes."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"A page I put in the menu from Custom pages is gone from it","s":"Put the page back with Add to menu in Custom pages, then reload Menu & content before you save there.","u":"menu/index.html#sym-1","x":"Menu & content was already open in another tab, and its save took the page out of the menu again."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"Menu & content only asks you to choose the event, or the event tags, in Events & updates","s":"Choose them in Events & updates and save, then pick an event in Event.","u":"menu/index.html#sym-2","x":"The app's event, or for an app with several events its event tags, is not chosen yet."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"My changes disappeared when I picked another event or language","s":"Make the changes again, and save before you switch.","u":"menu/index.html#sym-3","x":"In Menu & content, Sign-in & registration and Events & updates, switching the event or the language drops unsaved changes without asking."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"What I want to add is not in Add to this section","s":"Look for the item in the section, perhaps marked “Hidden”; a feature not switched on for the event, or a kind of page with no free place, cannot be added here.","u":"menu/index.html#sym-4","x":"It offers only the features switched on for the event and not already in the section, and A custom page or A documents page only while the event has a free place of that kind."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"Saving the menu says “Every menu item needs a name”","s":"Press Edit on that item, give it a name, and save again.","u":"menu/index.html#sym-5","x":"An item has no name, for example a page from Custom pages that Menu & content shows as “Page title”, so the menu was not saved."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"The Bottom bar switches are greyed out, or App Studio says “At most 4 items fit in the bottom navigation”","s":"Switch items off until four or fewer are on, then save; to add another tab, switch one off first.","u":"menu/index.html#sym-6","x":"All four places are taken, a hidden item with Bottom bar on included, or more are on, for example items taken over from the old App Builder."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"An item does not show for some people","s":"Check its row for “Hidden” or “Limited to some people”, a custom page's window for Only for people who are not signed in, and the menu in the preview with View as.","u":"menu/index.html#sym-7","x":"It is hidden, limited under Visible for, a custom page shown to guests only, or in a section those people do not see."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"There is no phone preview beside the menu","s":"Open Menu & content on a wide screen.","u":"menu/index.html#sym-8","x":"The preview shows only on wide screens."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Build the menu and content","t":"A saved change does not show on phones yet","s":"Check that App Studio said “Saved”, then look on a test build of this app from Build & test after its next refresh.","u":"menu/index.html#sym-9","x":"Installed builds of this app get saved changes the next time they refresh; an app made before App Studio never gets them, and a phone without a build of this app has nothing to refresh."},{"k":"Journey","t":"Get people using the app","s":"From a widget's switch to the new version that carries it, and from your game's wording to drawing the prize.","u":"engage/index.html","x":"The home-screen widgets you chose ship in a new version of your app, and your event runs Play & Win and you draw the prize from its entries."},{"k":"Step 1","j":"Get people using the app","t":"In Home-screen widgets, press a widget's switch so that it reads On.","s":"App Studio confirms with the widget's name and “is on. It ships with your next build.”","u":"engage/index.html#step-widget-on","x":"A widget you switch on ships with your next build, so people can add it to their phone's home screen. The switch saves at once, with the widget's last saved counters and colours, never unsaved ones. Ask the assistant needs the app's AI assistant, which your ExpoPlatform team switches on; until then App Studio warns that this widget “would have nothing to open”. Switching a widget off works the same way: your next build leaves it out, so people cannot add it to their home screen. App Studio confirms with the widget's name and “is on. It ships with your next build.” The Event stats switch, reading Off"},{"k":"Step 2","j":"Get people using the app","t":"For Event stats, while it is on, choose up to three counters, in order, and press Save changes.","s":"App Studio says “Widgets saved”.","u":"engage/index.html#step-counters","x":"Event stats shows up to three counters, in your order, and each person sees their own numbers. Three counters are chosen at first, so the other buttons are hidden: remove one to add another (“Up to 3 counters. Remove one to swap it.”). With no counter chosen, Save changes is held back: add one (“Choose at least one counter.”). These are not the counters of the Stats at a glance block on the app's Home screen, which has its own list, set per event. App Studio says “Widgets saved”. Counters, in order, with the three default counters"},{"k":"Step 3","j":"Get people using the app","t":"Under each widget's Colours, choose Light or dark or Brand colour, and press Save changes.","s":"The preview shows a Light and a Dark card, or one Brand colour card, and you pressed Save changes.","u":"engage/index.html#step-colours","x":"Light or dark follows the phone's light or dark mode, and Brand colour gives the widget your brand colour. Colours can be changed only while the widget is on. The preview shows a Light and a Dark card, or one Brand colour card, and you pressed Save changes. Colours for My agenda, with the Light and Dark preview cards"},{"k":"Step 4","j":"Get people using the app","t":"Make a new build in Build & test, check it on your phone, and publish it as a new version.","s":"The new version's release reads Live on Releases.","u":"engage/index.html#step-new-version","x":"A new version goes the same way as your first: build, test, Submit to the stores, ExpoPlatform's approval, the store's review and the rollout. A later iPhone version, and Android beyond its first 5%, wait for your ExpoPlatform team to start the rollout: ask your ExpoPlatform contact. On iPhone, the set-up step “Home-screen widgets ready” in Publish is done by your ExpoPlatform team, or by a signed iOS build, and does not block a release. The new version's release reads Live on Releases. The Build & test button at the top of every page of your app"},{"k":"Step 5","j":"Get people using the app","t":"In Play & Win, under Texts, read each screen's wording, one language at a time, change what you want, and save.","s":"Each card you changed shows how many texts are yours, such as “1 edited”, and you pressed Save Play & Win.","u":"engage/index.html#step-texts","x":"Your text replaces the app's own wording in that language only; texts you leave alone keep the app's wording. With several events, pick the event in Event first: Save Play & Win saves the selected event only. Consent holds the separate consent an attendee ticks before the vote is sent: changing it, in any language, makes a new consent version once you save. A text marked No default shows nothing in that language: type your own text for it. Each card you changed shows how many texts are yours, such as “1 edited”, and you pressed Save Play & Win. Texts, with the language box and the Voting screen card"},{"k":"Step 6","j":"Get people using the app","t":"Under Picture and link, upload your picture, add a “Book a meeting” link if you want one, and save.","s":"Your picture's thumbnail shows under Picture, and you saved.","u":"engage/index.html#step-picture","x":"Your picture replaces the trophy cups, and the final screen's Book a meeting button opens your link outside the app. The picture is stored as soon as it is uploaded, or fetched from a link you paste in Or paste a link to a picture, but this event uses it only after Save Play & Win. With no link, the final screen shows no Book a meeting button. Your picture's thumbnail shows under Picture, and you saved. Picture, with Upload, beside the “Book a meeting” link"},{"k":"Step 7","j":"Get people using the app","t":"In Play & Win, switch Play & Win on for your event and press Save Play & Win.","s":"App Studio says “Play & Win saved — attendees get it the next time they open the page”.","u":"engage/index.html#step-switch","x":"Signed-in attendees then see Play & Win in the event's menu, as long as Play & Win is in that menu. With several events, pick the event in Event first: Save Play & Win saves the selected event only. App Studio says “Play & Win saved — attendees get it the next time they open the page”. The Play & Win switch at the top of Play & Win"},{"k":"Step 8","j":"Get people using the app","t":"Check that Play & Win is in the event's menu, in Menu & content.","s":"You see Play & Win in the event's menu in Menu & content.","u":"engage/index.html#step-menu","x":"The app's menu shows the Play & Win row only to signed-in people, only when the event's menu carries the row, and only while the campaign is on. Menu & content shows one event at a time, and switching the event drops unsaved changes without asking: save first. If it is not there, ask your ExpoPlatform contact to add it. You see Play & Win in the event's menu in Menu & content. Menu & content in the sidebar"},{"k":"Step 9","j":"Get people using the app","t":"Switch Test mode on and save, then try voting in the app while signed in.","s":"Your test vote shows in Entries after you press Refresh.","u":"engage/index.html#step-test","x":"Voting then opens before the event starts, and still closes when the event ends. Test mode opens voting for everyone who can see Play & Win, not only for you. A vote made while testing is a real entry: it shows in Entries and counts as that person's one entry for the event. If voting should then wait for the event, switch Test mode off and save again. Your test vote shows in Entries after you press Refresh. Test mode, under the Play & Win switch"},{"k":"Step 10","j":"Get people using the app","t":"Under Kiosk (stand iPad), switch Kiosk on and press Save Play & Win.","s":"The QR code and the Kiosk link show, without the Save to activate badge.","u":"engage/index.html#step-kiosk-on","x":"Switching it on creates the kiosk's private link and its QR code, and the link works once you save. As App Studio says, “Anyone with this link can enter the draw from it, so share it only with the stand team.” Play & Win itself must be on too: while it is off, the kiosk shows “Voting is closed”. The kiosk has its own consent, separate from the app's: unless you reword it in Consent text, under Kiosk (stand iPad), the English one reads “By playing Play & Win you agree to receive emails about the prize draw.” The QR code and the Kiosk link show, without the Save to activate badge. The Kiosk switch, off; switched on, it shows the QR code and the Kiosk link"},{"k":"Step 11","j":"Get people using the app","t":"On the iPad, scan the QR code, add the page to the Home Screen and lock the iPad to it with Guided Access.","s":"Play & Win runs full screen on the iPad, from its Home Screen.","u":"engage/index.html#step-ipad","x":"Kiosk votes are real entries: they show in Entries with the source Kiosk. If the iPad shows “This page is not available.”, check that Kiosk is on and saved, and that the iPad opened the current link. A new link, made with New link and saved, replaces the old one, which then stops working: scan the new QR code on the iPad. To pause the kiosk, switch Kiosk off and save; switching it on again brings back the same link. Play & Win runs full screen on the iPad, from its Home Screen. Setting up the stand iPad Open the link in Safari on the iPad: scan the QR code with its camera. Tap Share, then Add to Home Screen, and start Play & Win from the Home Screen: it runs full screen, in portrait or landscape. Lock the iPad to it with Guided Access (Settings, Accessibility, Guided Access; then triple-click the top button), and set Display & Brightness, Auto-Lock to Never while the stand is open. After each vote the page clears itself for the next visitor after 20 seconds."},{"k":"Step 12","j":"Get people using the app","t":"Under Result, switch Campaign finished on, type the Actual number and press Save Play & Win.","s":"You saved with Campaign finished on and the actual number filled in.","u":"engage/index.html#step-finish","x":"Voting closes, and attendees who voted see their guess beside the actual number on the final screen. If App Studio says “Fix the highlighted fields before saving.”, fill in or correct the number: a whole number, digits only, up to 999,999,999, such as 13050. You saved with Campaign finished on and the actual number filled in. Campaign finished, under Result"},{"k":"Step 13","j":"Get people using the app","t":"Before the draw, delete each test entry with its trash button in Entries, then Delete entry.","s":"The list reloads without the entry.","u":"engage/index.html#step-clean","x":"Votes made while testing, in the app or on the kiosk, are real entries until you delete them. Deleting cannot be undone: the entry leaves the prize draw for good. The list reloads without the entry. Keep it Delete entry"},{"k":"Step 14","j":"Get people using the app","t":"In Entries, press Refresh, then Download CSV for the prize draw.","s":"A file named play-win-[event]-[date].csv is on your computer.","u":"engage/index.html#step-download","x":"The file lists every entry of the event, from the app or the kiosk, whatever the attendee's Networking setting. Entries are deleted three weeks (21 days) after the event ends: download them before then. A file named play-win-[event]-[date].csv is on your computer. Refresh Download CSV"},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Get people using the app","t":"Ask the assistant warns that the AI assistant is not switched on","s":"Ask your ExpoPlatform contact.","u":"engage/index.html#sym-1","x":"The app's AI assistant is set by your ExpoPlatform team, and without it this widget “would have nothing to open”."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Get people using the app","t":"People cannot add a widget you switched on to their home screen","s":"Make a new build in Build & test and publish it as a new version; phones show the change once it is installed, and to have people on older versions asked, or made, to update, ask your ExpoPlatform contact.","u":"engage/index.html#sym-2","x":"A widget ships with your next build: phones need a build made after you switched it on."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Get people using the app","t":"The phone preview does not show my wording","s":"Save your texts: as App Studio says, “Attendees get it the next time they open Play & Win.”","u":"engage/index.html#sym-3","x":"The preview beside the page always shows Play & Win with the app's default texts and voting open, whatever you set."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Get people using the app","t":"Attendees do not see Play & Win in the app","s":"Check that Play & Win is on and saved for that event, and that it is in that event's menu in Menu & content; if it is not, ask your ExpoPlatform contact; people see it only once they are signed in.","u":"engage/index.html#sym-4","x":"The app shows the Play & Win row only to signed-in people, only when the event's menu carries the row, and only while the campaign is on."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Get people using the app","t":"People cannot vote, in the app or on the kiosk","s":"Switch Play & Win on and save; to open voting before the event starts, switch Test mode on and save.","u":"engage/index.html#sym-5","x":"Voting is open during the event's own dates, or earlier while Test mode is on, and never once the campaign is finished; the kiosk also needs Play & Win itself on."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Get people using the app","t":"The iPad shows “This page is not available.” instead of the game","s":"Check that Kiosk is on and saved, and that the iPad opened the current link: after New link, save and scan the new QR code.","u":"engage/index.html#sym-6","x":"The link is wrong, the kiosk is off or not saved, or the app is archived; the page never says which."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Get people using the app","t":"“This email has already played.” shows on the kiosk","s":"One e-mail plays once per event, in the app or on the kiosk: that e-mail's entry is already in Entries.","u":"engage/index.html#sym-7","x":"The typed e-mail already has an entry for this event, from the app or the kiosk."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Get people using the app","t":"The iPad shows “Couldn't load Play & Win”","s":"Check the iPad's connection: as the page says, “Check the connection. The page tries again by itself.”","u":"engage/index.html#sym-8","x":"The page could not reach the server; it tries again every 15 seconds."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Get people using the app","t":"“Fix the highlighted fields before saving.” shows when you press Save Play & Win","s":"Correct the highlighted field, then save: the actual number is a whole number, digits only, up to 999,999,999, and the link a full web address, or empty.","u":"engage/index.html#sym-9","x":"The actual number or the Book a meeting link has a problem."},{"k":"Journey","t":"Change content during the event","s":"From a change you need during the event to installed apps showing it, with no new version.","u":"live/index.html","x":"Installed apps show your changes to the menu, the home screen, pages and texts, for the right event and language, with no new version."},{"k":"Step 1","j":"Change content during the event","t":"Know which changes reach installed apps by themselves, and which need a new version.","s":"You know which of your changes need a new version.","u":"live/index.html#step-know","x":"Changes to the menu, the home screen, pages and texts need no new build. Name, icon & splash shows the same save-bar line as the other sections, but phones show the icon, the name under it (in store builds, the store name), and the splash picture and its colour only after a new build is installed. A home-screen widget's switch saves at once, with no save button, and reaches phones only with your next build. You know which of your changes need a new version. Reaches installed apps by itself Colours & fonts, Home screen, Menu & content and Custom pages: at the next refresh Sign-in & registration: at the next refresh Texts in Translations: within about 30 minutes Your choice of events in Events & updates: no new build What a home-screen widget shows: no new build Play & Win: no new build Needs a new build and store release The app icon The name under the icon (in store builds, the store name) The splash picture and its colour Switching a home-screen widget on or off"},{"k":"Step 2","j":"Change content during the event","t":"Open App Studio from your admin, then your app, and the section you want to change.","s":"The section is open, with your app's name in the top bar.","u":"live/index.html#step-open","x":"The menu on the left holds every section: Menu & content under App, and Home screen, Custom pages and Translations under Look. A session lasts up to 8 hours: when it ends, open App Studio again from your admin and make again any change that was not saved. If an amber bar says “This page is from an older deployment, so saving does nothing”, copy out what you typed, press Reload in the bar and make the change again. The section is open, with your app's name in the top bar. The sections of your app, in the menu on the left of every page"},{"k":"Step 3","j":"Change content during the event","t":"Pick the event and the language you are changing, before you change anything.","s":"The section shows the event and the language you want to change.","u":"live/index.html#step-event","x":"In apps with several events, Home screen has an event select and Custom pages an event picker; the home's header texts and Custom pages pick the language with buttons such as EN and DE, and Translations has Language at the top of its list. In Menu & content, Sign-in & registration and Events & updates, switching the event or the language drops unsaved changes without asking: save first. Language of the texts starts on English each time you open the section. In Sign-in & registration, only the button texts are kept per language: the sign-in mode, the addresses and the switches change for every language. The section shows the event and the language you want to change. Event Language of the texts"},{"k":"Step 4","j":"Change content during the event","t":"In Menu & content, rename, hide, move or add the event's menu items.","s":"You pressed Save or Save changes, App Studio says “Saved”, and the phone preview shows the menu you want.","u":"live/index.html#step-menu","x":"The change is for this event only, and item names are kept per language. Save in an item's window saves the event's whole menu at once, with your other unsaved changes on the page. Remove from the menu does not ask first, and once saved the item is gone in every language with its content: to keep it in App Studio, hide it instead. A change made in an item's window shows in the phone preview only after its Save: check it then with View as. You pressed Save or Save changes, App Studio says “Saved”, and the phone preview shows the menu you want. Section header Bottom bar Add to this section Move up Move down Edit Remove from the menu Add"},{"k":"Step 5","j":"Change content during the event","t":"In Home screen, add, hide, move or change the event's blocks.","s":"The phone preview shows the home you want, and after Save home screen App Studio says “Content saved — live on the next app fetch”.","u":"live/index.html#step-home","x":"Each event has its own home, and Save home screen saves every event you edited since the last save. Restore the default home is saved straight away, without Save home screen. A block's bin takes it off the list at once, without asking: to keep its settings, switch the block off instead. The phone shows your unsaved home on sample content. The phone preview shows the home you want, and after Save home screen App Studio says “Content saved — live on the next app fetch”. Blocks: what the home shows, in order"},{"k":"Step 6","j":"Change content during the event","t":"In Custom pages, change or write the event's page, and press Save page.","s":"The phone preview shows your page, and the save bar reads “Live on the next app refresh. No new build needed.”","u":"live/index.html#step-page","x":"Each page belongs to one event, and a saved page is “Live on the next app refresh. No new build needed.” If someone else, such as your ExpoPlatform team, saved the page after you opened it, your save is refused: copy your text, reload, open the page again and make the change again. When you press Add to menu or add a built-in screen in Custom pages, reload any other tab showing Menu & content before you save there, or that save takes it out again. Who sees it does not protect a page: “everything on a page can be read by anyone who has your app.” The phone preview shows your page, and the save bar reads “Live on the next app refresh. No new build needed.” Discard Save page"},{"k":"Step 7","j":"Change content during the event","t":"In Translations, choose the language, find the text, type your wording and press the save button.","s":"App Studio says “Saved. Installed apps pick the texts up within about 30 minutes.”","u":"live/index.html#step-text","x":"Installed apps pick up saved texts within about 30 minutes, with no new build; Translations has no phone preview. Your wording applies to every event of the app, not to one event. Menu names and the sign-in and registration button texts are not here: change them per event in Menu & content and Sign-in & registration. To undo your wording, empty the field or press the arrow beside it, and save. App Studio says “Saved. Installed apps pick the texts up within about 30 minutes.” Translations Change any text the app shows, in each language. Leave a field empty to keep the standard text. No new build is needed."},{"k":"Step 8","j":"Change content during the event","t":"Check the change in the app on a phone: it shows at the next refresh, and texts within about 30 minutes.","s":"A phone with a build of this app shows your change.","u":"live/index.html#step-reach","x":"The app checks for new texts when it opens, when it comes back to the foreground and every 5 minutes while open, at most once every 30 minutes. A change to the menu, the home's blocks or a page shows only in the event you saved it for; your wording in Translations shows in every event. A picture or video you upload is stored at once, but the app uses it only after you save. Your old apps never show what you save in Menu & content, Sign-in & registration or Events & updates: check every change on a phone with a build of this app, a test build from Build & test first. A phone with a build of this app shows your change. Menu & content Saved Changes reach the app the next time it refreshes."},{"k":"Step 9","j":"Change content during the event","t":"For the icon, the splash picture or colour, or a widget switch, build a new version in Build & test.","s":"Each new build ends Ready and reads Store-signed; if a ready build is not Store-signed, ask your ExpoPlatform contact to add your app's store key.","u":"live/index.html#step-version","x":"Phones show these only after the next build is installed: a test build first, then a store release from Publish. In store builds, the name under the icon is the store name, not App name in the app, so a new build does not change it: ask your ExpoPlatform contact. After the stores' review, a later version waits for your ExpoPlatform team to start the rollout (on Android, after a first 5%): ask your ExpoPlatform contact. Whether people with an older version are asked, or made, to update is set by your ExpoPlatform team: ask your ExpoPlatform contact. Each new build ends Ready and reads Store-signed; if a ready build is not Store-signed, ask your ExpoPlatform contact to add your app's store key. The Build & test button at the top of every page of your app"},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Change content during the event","t":"App Studio says “Your session has expired - reopen App Studio from your admin” or “Reopen App Studio from your admin”","s":"Open App Studio again from your ExpoPlatform admin, then make the change again and save it.","u":"live/index.html#sym-1","x":"Your App Studio session has ended, or could not start, and a save refused for that reason is not carried out."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Change content during the event","t":"My changes disappeared when I picked another event or language","s":"Make the changes again, and save before you switch.","u":"live/index.html#sym-2","x":"In Menu & content, Sign-in & registration and Events & updates, switching the event or the language drops unsaved changes without asking."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Change content during the event","t":"A renamed menu item keeps its old name in another language","s":"Pick each language in Language of the texts, rename the item there too, and save before you switch.","u":"live/index.html#sym-3","x":"Item names are kept per language, and you renamed it in one."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Change content during the event","t":"Saving the menu says “Every menu item needs a name”","s":"Press Edit on that item, give it a name, and save again.","u":"live/index.html#sym-4","x":"An item has no name, for example a page from Custom pages that Menu & content shows as “Page title”, so the menu was not saved."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Change content during the event","t":"The phone preview says “Live preview crashed” or “The app's config could not be loaded…”","s":"For “Live preview crashed”, press Retry; for the second message, try again in a minute.","u":"live/index.html#sym-5","x":"The app inside the preview stopped with an error, or the event server is not answering, so the preview cannot start."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Change content during the event","t":"Saving a page says “This page was changed by someone else — reload it before saving”","s":"Copy any text you want to keep, reload the page, open your page again and make your changes again.","u":"live/index.html#sym-6","x":"Someone else, such as your ExpoPlatform team, saved the page after you opened it."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Change content during the event","t":"The text I want to change is not in Translations","s":"Change them there; for any other text, search with other words or with the text's key.","u":"live/index.html#sym-7","x":"Menu names and the sign-in and registration button texts are worded per event, in Menu & content and Sign-in & registration."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Change content during the event","t":"My change does not show on phones yet","s":"Check that the section shows your change for the right event and language, that you saved it, and that the phone has a build of this app; for a text, allow about 30 minutes.","u":"live/index.html#sym-8","x":"A saved change shows at the next refresh, and a text within about 30 minutes, on a phone with a build of this app; a change you have not saved never reaches it, and your old apps never show what you save in Menu & content, Sign-in & registration or Events & updates."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Change content during the event","t":"My new icon, name, splash picture or widget does not show on phones","s":"For the icon, the splash picture and its colour or a widget switch, make a new build, install it and publish it; for the name in store builds, ask your ExpoPlatform contact.","u":"live/index.html#sym-9","x":"They reach phones only with a new build, and so does switching a widget on or off; in store builds, the name under the icon is the store name, not App name in the app."},{"k":"Journey","t":"Release a new version","s":"From changes that need a new build to people getting the new version, for an app already in the stores.","u":"update/index.html","x":"A new version of your app, tried on real phones first, has passed the stores' review and is rolling out to people."},{"k":"Planner","j":"Release a new version","t":"Plan from the date the new version should reach people","s":"Enter the date the new version should reach people, and the plan works back to the working day each step should be done by. The days are allowances you can change, and your ExpoPlatform team confirms the dates of their own steps. Working days are Monday to Friday: public holidays are not counted.","u":"update/index.html#plan","x":"plan planner dates deadline timeline schedule The new version should reach people by Plan your release Changes for the new version saved New builds sent to your testers The review check clear Ask ExpoPlatform to publish ExpoPlatform approves the request The stores review the new version Your ExpoPlatform team starts the rollout The new version reaches people"},{"k":"Step 1","j":"Release a new version","t":"Check whether your changes need a new version, or reach installed apps by themselves.","s":"You know which of your changes need a new version.","u":"update/index.html#step-need","x":"Phones show a change to what is built into the app only after the next build is installed: a test build first, then a store release. You know which of your changes need a new version. Reaches installed apps by itself Colours & fonts, Home screen, Menu & content and Custom pages: at the next refresh Sign-in & registration: at the next refresh Texts in Translations: within about 30 minutes Your choice of events in Events & updates: no new build What a home-screen widget shows: no new build Play & Win: no new build Needs a new build and store release The app icon The name under the icon (in store builds, the store name) The splash picture and its colour Switching a home-screen widget on or off"},{"k":"Step 2","j":"Release a new version","t":"Make and save every change the new version should carry, before you build.","s":"Every change the new version should carry is saved.","u":"update/index.html#step-save","x":"A build takes the icon and the splash picture and its colour from your app's settings at the time it is made. A home-screen widget's switch saves at once, with no save button, and switching it on or off reaches phones with your next build. In store builds, the name under the icon is the app's store name, not App name in the app: ask your ExpoPlatform contact about the store name. Every change the new version should carry is saved. Name, icon & splash"},{"k":"Step 3","j":"Release a new version","t":"In Build & test, press Build for iOS, then Build for Android.","s":"Each build ends Ready and reads Store-signed; if a ready build is not Store-signed, ask your ExpoPlatform contact to add your app's store key.","u":"update/index.html#step-build","x":"Each build is made from the app code ExpoPlatform deploys, with your app's settings at the time of the build. For Android, keep App Bundle (AAB): Google Play accepts only an App Bundle. Each build ends Ready and reads Store-signed; if a ready build is not Store-signed, ask your ExpoPlatform contact to add your app's store key. The Build & test button at the top of every page of your app"},{"k":"Step 4","j":"Release a new version","t":"Under Send to testers, send each new build to your testers, and try it on real phones.","s":"You and your testers have tried the new version: on iPhone, the send shows Live on TestFlight.","u":"update/index.html#step-testers","x":"Sending needs no approval from ExpoPlatform, and on TestFlight “Apple checks the build first, usually within a day.” Each platform takes one release at a time, store releases included: while your last version of a platform is still moving, you cannot send a build of that platform. An amber Staged on Play badge means the Android release waits as a draft in Google Play Console until it is published there: ask your ExpoPlatform contact. With a demo account saved in Publish, a TestFlight send first checks that its demo event is ready for review. You and your testers have tried the new version: on iPhone, the send shows Live on TestFlight. Where should the build go? TestFlight TestFlight Google Play internal testing Add testers Build Send"},{"k":"Step 5","j":"Release a new version","t":"Ask your ExpoPlatform contact what each store will show as What's new for this version.","s":"You know what each store will show as What's new for this version.","u":"update/index.html#step-whatsnew","x":"App Studio does not send your What's new to either store: a Google Play release made from your request carries a standard note, “This update contains performance and stability updates.” Copy, under For the store's “What's new” in a build's Details, only copies the lines: nothing is saved or sent to the stores. You know what each store will show as What's new for this version. Google Play, with a new version Your new pictures Not your texts Not your What's new: a standard note instead A later App Store version App name, Short description and Privacy policy link Not your What's new, your other texts or your new pictures"},{"k":"Step 6","j":"Release a new version","t":"Under Store review, press Check again, and fix anything marked Your move.","s":"Store review reads Ready for review.","u":"update/index.html#step-reviewcheck","x":"Store reviewers sign in to your app with this account, and a release waits at Ready while Store review has something to sort out. If it says “The demo event looks empty”, pick a demo event with at least 3 sessions on its agenda, or add sessions to it. If it says “The demo event could not be checked”, check the login, the password and the event number, and save them again. Store review reads Ready for review. Demo login Demo password Demo event number Notes for the reviewers Check again Save demo account"},{"k":"Step 7","j":"Release a new version","t":"On Releases, press Submit to the stores, keep each store's newest build, and press Submit.","s":"App Studio says “Sent to ExpoPlatform for approval”, or “Sent to the stores” for an app that needs no approval.","u":"update/index.html#step-submit","x":"Each store with a finished build starts ticked, with its newest build chosen. Let each send to your testers finish first: a request approved while a test send of the same platform is still on its way cannot start. App Studio says “Sent to ExpoPlatform for approval”, or “Sent to the stores” for an app that needs no approval. App Store Build Google Play Build Close Submit"},{"k":"Step 8","j":"Release a new version","t":"Your ExpoPlatform team approves the request.","s":"Releases says “Approved [when]: [the builds] went to the stores' review. Follow it below.”","u":"update/index.html#step-approve","x":"When they approve, your store listing is sent, and each build goes on to its store's review. A declined request reads “Declined: [reason]”, or “Declined: no reason given”: sort out what the reason names and submit again, or ask your ExpoPlatform contact when no reason is given. Releases says “Approved [when]: [the builds] went to the stores' review. Follow it below.” Releases Waiting for ExpoPlatform approval: App Store [version], Google Play [version], sent [when]."},{"k":"Step 9","j":"Release a new version","t":"Apple and Google review the new version; follow it on Releases.","s":"The release reads Approved.","u":"update/index.html#step-review","x":"Apple typically reviews 90% of submissions in less than 48 hours; for certain developer accounts, Google Play's review can take up to seven days, or longer in exceptional cases. If a store turns the release down, its card shows the store's message when it gave one, and a new release goes through Submit to the stores and ExpoPlatform's approval again. Cancel release does not take a release out of the store's review: App Studio stops following it, and a review in progress carries on. If your event is close and the iPhone version is still in review, your ExpoPlatform team can ask Apple to expedite the review, and Apple decides. The release reads Approved. Draft Uploading Processing Ready Submitted In review Approved Rolling out Live"},{"k":"Step 10","j":"Release a new version","t":"Your ExpoPlatform team starts the rollout; follow it on Rollout.","s":"The release reads Rolling out, and Live once everyone can get this version.","u":"update/index.html#step-rollout","x":"Only an app's first iPhone version and Android's first 5% stage go out by themselves: later iPhone versions, and Android beyond 5%, wait for your ExpoPlatform team. What now says “The rollout starts on its own and reaches people step by step.”, but for a later version that holds only for Android's first 5% stage: ask your ExpoPlatform contact. If What now says “The rollout is stopped”, ExpoPlatform is looking at it: ask your ExpoPlatform contact. The release reads Rolling out, and Live once everyone can get this version. App Store Approved by the store The rollout starts on its own and reaches people step by step. Open rollout"},{"k":"Step 11","j":"Release a new version","t":"On Your apps, check which version people can download from each store.","s":"The first badge names your new version, such as “Live · 1.94.4”.","u":"update/index.html#step-live","x":"Under App Store and Google Play, the first badge is what people can download now, and a second badge, when there is one, shows the newest release on its way. A second badge reading Approved means the release passed the store's review and waits for your ExpoPlatform team to start the rollout. The first badge names your new version, such as “Live · 1.94.4”. Your apps, with each app's store badges"},{"k":"Step 12","j":"Release a new version","t":"Your ExpoPlatform team sets the update rules, if older versions should be asked, or made, to update.","s":"App updates on your app's Overview shows the rules you asked for.","u":"update/index.html#step-prompts","x":"Below the Must update version, people must update before they can use the app; below Asked to update, they are asked and may skip it. These rules are set by your ExpoPlatform team: to change a rule or the wording of a prompt, ask your ExpoPlatform contact. A rule for a version that is not fully live in that store yet waits, and the app is told the rule only once that version is fully live. App updates on your app's Overview shows the rules you asked for. App updates Older versions are asked, or made, to update when the app starts."},{"k":"Step 13","j":"Release a new version","t":"In Analytics, open the Devices tab to see which versions phones run.","s":"Your new version shows under Versions, with its installs.","u":"update/index.html#step-versions","x":"Versions counts the installs on each version of your app over the last 30 days, each install once, under the version it reported last. Your new version shows under Versions, with its installs. The Devices tab, with its Versions chart"},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Release a new version","t":"My new icon, name, splash picture or widget does not show on phones","s":"For the icon, the splash picture and its colour or a widget switch, make a new build, install it and publish it; for the name in store builds, ask your ExpoPlatform contact.","u":"update/index.html#sym-1","x":"They reach phones only with a new build, and so does switching a widget on or off; in store builds, the name under the icon is the store name, not App name in the app."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Release a new version","t":"A choice in Send to testers is greyed out","s":"Read the reason the dialog gives and do what it says; if new builds are not Store-signed, or a release waits as a draft in Google Play Console, ask your ExpoPlatform contact; while another release is still moving, wait until it has finished.","u":"update/index.html#sym-2","x":"The app is not in that store yet, there is no Store-signed build of that platform, another release of that platform is still moving (a store release included), or, on Android, an earlier release waits as a draft or the newest build is already on another Google Play track."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Release a new version","t":"A TestFlight send says “Failed to submit release”","s":"Check the demo account under Store review in Publish, then press Send again: it continues the same release.","u":"update/index.html#sym-3","x":"The release was created but not sent; with a demo account saved in Publish, its demo event may not be ready for review, or its saved login cannot be used."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Release a new version","t":"A release is stuck at Ready","s":"Open Store review in Publish and fix each item marked Your move; items marked Our team are your ExpoPlatform team's.","u":"update/index.html#sym-4","x":"Store review still has something to sort out, such as a missing demo account, a demo account the check cannot sign in with, or a demo event that looks empty."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Release a new version","t":"Releases says “Approved, but the stores could not take it yet”","s":"Nothing: ExpoPlatform is on it.","u":"update/index.html#sym-5","x":"ExpoPlatform approved, but publishing could not start: each platform takes one release at a time, and another release of that platform, such as a test send, was still on its way."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Release a new version","t":"A store turned the release down","s":"Fix it, build again if needed, and ask again with Submit to the stores: the new release goes through ExpoPlatform's approval and the store's review again.","u":"update/index.html#sym-6","x":"The store found a problem; its card shows the store's message when it gave one."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Release a new version","t":"The store approved the new version, but it is not reaching people","s":"Ask your ExpoPlatform contact.","u":"update/index.html#sym-7","x":"Later iPhone versions, and Android beyond its first 5% stage, wait for your ExpoPlatform team to start the rollout."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Release a new version","t":"What now says “The rollout is stopped”","s":"Ask your ExpoPlatform contact.","u":"update/index.html#sym-8","x":"The rollout was halted, and ExpoPlatform is looking at it."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"Release a new version","t":"People on older versions are not asked to update","s":"Check App updates on your app's Overview, and ask your ExpoPlatform contact to set or change a rule.","u":"update/index.html#sym-9","x":"App updates reads Off when no rule is set, and a rule for a version that is not fully live in that store yet waits until it is."},{"k":"Journey","t":"See how people use the app","s":"From a live app to numbers you can read, narrow and share.","u":"measure/index.html","x":"You can read how people used your app in a period: who opened it, what they looked at and which features they used, and you know how each number is counted."},{"k":"Step 1","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Open your app in App Studio, then Analytics under After launch in the sidebar.","s":"Analytics opens on Overview, with the last 30 days.","u":"measure/index.html#step-open","x":"Once your app is live, Analytics shows how it is used: who opens it, what they look at, which features they use and how fast it runs. The numbers come from the installed app, and a phone appears in Devices once it has opened a version of the app built in App Studio. Analytics opens on Overview, with the last 30 days. The Overview tab, ringed, here with 90 days chosen; Whole screen shows Analytics chosen in the sidebar under After launch"},{"k":"Step 2","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Under Period, press 7d, 14d, 30d or 90d, and under Event, choose an event or keep All events.","s":"The line beside the date button repeats your dates and the number of days.","u":"measure/index.html#step-choose","x":"A period is whole days in UTC, today included, and at most 92 days long. For other dates, press the date button, pick the first and the last day, and press Apply: closing the calendar drops them. With an event chosen, only what people did while that event was chosen in the app counts. The line beside the date button repeats your dates and the number of days. Event and Period at the top of Analytics"},{"k":"Step 3","j":"See how people use the app","t":"If a tab says “No activity in this period”, press Show the last 90 days or Clear filters when offered.","s":"The tab is read again with the longer period or without the filters.","u":"measure/index.html#step-empty","x":"A tab shows this only when nothing in it can be drawn. If neither button shows, choose other dates in the calendar, up to 92 days. Clear filters drops the event, platform and user type but keeps the period. Audience and Tech can show cards while other tabs are empty: some of their cards read the phones' own check-ins. The tab is read again with the longer period or without the filters. Analytics No activity in this period Numbers appear here as soon as people use the app. Try a longer period, or fewer filters."},{"k":"Step 4","j":"See how people use the app","t":"On Overview, read the six tiles against the days just before, then Daily activity below them.","s":"You know how each headline number moved against the days just before.","u":"measure/index.html#step-overview","x":"People, Signed in, Devices, Sessions, Avg. session and Screen views are each compared with the same number of days just before: green is better, red is worse. The days of Daily activity do not add up to the tiles: each day counts its own people. Someone who used the app before signing in, and then signed in during the same period, counts twice under People: once as the phone and once as the account. A session with a single action counts as 0 minutes and pulls Avg. session down. You know how each headline number moved against the days just before. Overview Previous period: [value] Same as the previous period Nothing to compare in the previous period"},{"k":"Step 5","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Press How to read at the top right to open the Analytics guide on the part for your tab.","s":"You read the entry named like the card you are looking at.","u":"measure/index.html#step-define","x":"Each entry is named like the card on screen and says what it shows, how it is counted and which app records it comes from. You read the entry named like the card you are looking at. How to read Export Refresh"},{"k":"Step 6","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Read Latest activity under the heading, and press Refresh to read the open tab again.","s":"You know when the newest activity was recorded, or that none was, and the open tab is read again.","u":"measure/index.html#step-fresh","x":"Latest activity says when the newest activity under your filters was recorded, from just now to a date once it is 14 days or more, or the line reads “No activity in this period yet”. Refresh reads only the open tab: another tab keeps the numbers it read for the same filters until you press Refresh there. The Analytics guide says a phone without a connection keeps its records for up to 30 days, so a period that has just ended can still grow a little. Data completeness on Tech, measured only with All events, shows the share of the phones' records that has arrived, and says “Some data still on its way” below 99%. You know when the newest activity was recorded, or that none was, and the open tab is read again. The line under the Analytics heading, here with nothing recorded in the period"},{"k":"Step 7","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Open Audience to see who people are, where they come from and whether they come back.","s":"You know where new installs came from and, day by day, how many devices were new or came back.","u":"measure/index.html#step-audience","x":"Install sources shows how each new install first opened the app: from a link, a QR code, the store with no link, or a link the app could not read. Installs and updates counts an install when the app is first opened, not when it is downloaded from the store. With one event chosen, new in New vs returning still means new to the app, not to that event. Where people are places phones by the network they use, so a phone on mobile data or a VPN can be placed in its operator's country. You know where new installs came from and, day by day, how many devices were new or came back. New vs returning, ringed at the top of the Audience tab, empty in this period, beside Languages"},{"k":"Step 8","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Open Engagement to see when people used the app, the screens and features they used, and their searches.","s":"You know which screens and features people used most.","u":"measure/index.html#step-engagement","x":"Searches flags a term when 25% or more of its searches found nothing. When people use the app shows each phone's local time, while the period is in UTC days, so its first and last hours can be cut differently. You know which screens and features people used most. Engagement Activity by weekday and hour. What people did in the app, and how many of them did it. Terms at least three people searched for."},{"k":"Step 9","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Open Content for the exhibitors, products, sessions, speakers, brands, documents and videos people looked at.","s":"You know which items people viewed most.","u":"measure/index.html#step-content","x":"Each row of the top table gives views, people, favourites, impressions and CTR; exhibitors add Booth located and Meetings asked, and sessions Added to agenda. CTR can pass 100%, because a profile can also be opened from search, a link or another profile. Favourites that were later removed still count in the top table; Favourites shows how many were removed. You know which items people viewed most. Content Views per impression in a list"},{"k":"Step 10","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Open Networking to see the meetings, messages, leads and personal agendas of the period.","s":"You know how many meetings were requested and accepted in the period.","u":"measure/index.html#step-networking","x":"Meetings follows requests to the meetings accepted and rated, and those declined, cancelled and rescheduled. Each meeting step counts what happened in the period, not one set of meetings followed through, so accepted can be more than requested. Meeting attendance shows 0% and “Low attendance” whenever a meeting was accepted, and Contact requests stays empty: the Analytics guide says the app does not offer a meeting check-in or contact requests yet. You know how many meetings were requested and accepted in the period. Networking From the request to the rating. Messages sent, chats started and chats people opened to read. Badges scanned in the app, and what became of the leads."},{"k":"Step 11","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Open Promotion to see how sponsor placements, push notifications, links and QR codes reached people.","s":"You know how often sponsor banners were seen and clicked, and how many pushes were opened.","u":"measure/index.html#step-promotion","x":"Sponsors gives the impressions, clicks and CTR of each sponsor in each place its banner was shown. The Analytics guide says a sponsor impression counts when at least half of the banner was on screen for at least a second, once per screen visit. The Analytics guide says Received misses pushes that arrived while the app was not on screen unless they were tapped, so the open rate can pass 100%, while Opened is complete. You know how often sponsor banners were seen and clicked, and how many pushes were opened. Promotion [n] clicks on sponsored places. Impressions per place in the app, with the click rate. QR codes scanned and downloaded in the app."},{"k":"Step 12","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Open Performance for speed and server answers, and Tech for versions, phones, permissions and reliability.","s":"You know how fast the app started and how reliably it worked in the period.","u":"measure/index.html#step-health","x":"Lower is better everywhere on Performance: Typical is the median, and Slowest 5% the 95th percentile. Errors people saw on Tech leaves out app crashes; your ExpoPlatform team can see more about the app's health, such as crashes and errors: ask your ExpoPlatform contact. You know how fast the app started and how reliably it worked in the period. Performance Cold: from tapping the icon to the first screen people can use. Warm: from coming back to the app to its first frame. The typical cold start, with the slowest 5% beside it. How the sampled calls to the server were answered."},{"k":"Step 13","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Open Devices to see the phones with your app, the versions they run and who is signed in on each.","s":"You see the install figures and the versions in use.","u":"measure/index.html#step-devices","x":"Versions shows which app versions phones ran over the last 30 days, and Show devices lists the phones on one of them. The dashboard's filters, Latest activity and Export do not apply here: use the tab's own Search, Platform, App version and Signed in filters. The list shows personal data: the name and email, or company, of the person signed in on each phone, and a city and country located from its network. You see the install figures and the versions in use. Installs, last 30 days, ringed among the Devices tab's install figures; Whole screen shows the tab chosen"},{"k":"Step 14","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Under Platform, choose iOS or Android, and under User type, choose Visitor, Exhibitor, Speaker or Guest.","s":"The open tab shows that slice, and Reset filters brings back every event, platform and user type and the last 30 days.","u":"measure/index.html#step-narrow","x":"Each choice applies at once: the open tab is read again, then the other tabs, and the filters stay as you switch tabs. Languages, Where people are, Top cities, Operating systems and Phones ignore the user type, and Data completeness and the people counts in the Event list ignore both. The Analytics guide says older app versions do not report the user type: their activity drops out as soon as you choose one. Filters are not saved: a reload of your admin's page in the same browser tab keeps them, but a new browser tab opens your list of apps. The open tab shows that slice, and Reset filters brings back every event, platform and user type and the last 30 days. Platform and User type, under Event"},{"k":"Step 15","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Press Export, choose a format and the sections, and press Make the PDF or Make the CSV files.","s":"“Your report is ready” shows, and Download PDF or Download ZIP saves the file.","u":"measure/index.html#step-export","x":"App Studio's own words: “Turn what you see into a branded report for your team, sponsors or exhibitors”. The file uses the filters set when you press Export: set Event, Period, Platform and User type first. The file can be downloaded for one hour from when it was made. If the dialog names a section it could not prepare, the file says it is missing: export again to include it. “Your report is ready” shows, and Download PDF or Download ZIP saves the file. Format PDF report PDF report CSV (Excel) Sections to include Make the PDF"},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"See how people use the app","t":"A tab says “No activity in this period”","s":"Press Show the last 90 days or Clear filters when offered; if neither shows, choose other dates in the calendar, up to 92 days.","u":"measure/index.html#sym-1","x":"Nothing in the tab can be drawn for your period and filters."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"See how people use the app","t":"A tab says “These numbers could not be loaded right now” instead of its cards","s":"Press Try again.","u":"measure/index.html#sym-2","x":"The tab could not be read."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"See how people use the app","t":"People is higher than Signed in and Devices suggest","s":"Nothing to fix: Signed in counts only accounts, and Devices counts installed copies of the app.","u":"measure/index.html#sym-3","x":"Someone who used the app before signing in, and then signed in during the same period, counts once as the phone and once as the account."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"See how people use the app","t":"The numbers seem older than they should be","s":"Press Refresh on that tab, then read Latest activity again.","u":"measure/index.html#sym-4","x":"A tab keeps the numbers it read for the same filters until you press Refresh there, and Latest activity does not move on its own."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"See how people use the app","t":"The Devices tab ignores your filters","s":"Use its own Search, Platform, App version and Signed in filters.","u":"measure/index.html#sym-5","x":"Devices reads each phone's latest check-in, so the dashboard's filters, Latest activity and Export do not apply to it."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Some cards do not change when you choose a user type","s":"Nothing to fix: How the numbers are counted lists what each filter does not narrow.","u":"measure/index.html#sym-6","x":"Languages, Where people are, Top cities, Operating systems and Phones ignore the user type, and Data completeness and the people counts in the Event list always cover every user type."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Export says “The report could not be made. Your data is safe; try again in a minute.”","s":"Press Try again in a minute.","u":"measure/index.html#sym-7","x":"The export failed, and no file was made."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"See how people use the app","t":"A link does not open your view for a colleague","s":"Ask them to open Analytics from their own admin and choose the same tab and filters, or send them an export.","u":"measure/index.html#sym-8","x":"App Studio opens only inside each person's own ExpoPlatform admin, so a link cannot open the view."},{"k":"Something's wrong","j":"See how people use the app","t":"Export says “This report is no longer kept”","s":"Press Try again and make the report again.","u":"measure/index.html#sym-9","x":"The file was kept for one hour and is gone."},{"k":"Journey","t":"Fix a problem","s":"What App Studio's messages mean, and what to do when something does not work.","u":"fix/index.html","x":"You know what went wrong and what to do about it, and when to ask your ExpoPlatform team."},{"k":"Step 1","j":"Fix a problem","t":"Note what App Studio says, word for word, and where it says it.","s":"You have the message's words, or you know which step of a journey you are on.","u":"fix/index.html#step-read","x":"The guide's search finds most messages by a few of their words. You have the message's words, or you know which step of a journey you are on."},{"k":"Step 2","j":"Fix a problem","t":"Pick what you see from the problems below.","s":"You found your problem, or none of them fits.","u":"fix/index.html#step-pick","x":"Each problem says why it happens and what to do, and opens the journey step it belongs to. You found your problem, or none of them fits."},{"k":"Step 3","j":"Fix a problem","t":"Not listed? Find the message on Messages, word for word in the guide.","s":"You found the message and the section it shows in.","u":"fix/index.html#step-messages","x":"It lists App Studio's messages by section, with where each one shows. You found the message and the section it shows in."},{"k":"Step 4","j":"Fix a problem","t":"If a picture or a text was refused, check Limits, sizes and formats in the guide.","s":"You know the limit the field has.","u":"fix/index.html#step-limits","x":"It lists every limit App Studio puts on a field, by section. You know the limit the field has."},{"k":"Step 5","j":"Fix a problem","t":"If App Studio leaves it to your ExpoPlatform team, ask your ExpoPlatform contact.","s":"You asked your ExpoPlatform contact about the item, by its name in the guide.","u":"fix/index.html#step-team","x":"Set by your ExpoPlatform team lists what App Studio does not let you change, by section. You asked your ExpoPlatform contact about the item, by its name in the guide."}];
